 VERDICT: on strong tournaments the two 'centrality rankings' are compared for the first time.
 If they agree everywhere -> they are the SAME ranking (one theorem); if they diverge -> two
 genuinely different centralities (Perron/spectral vs arborescence/combinatorial), and the
 divergence set is a new object. Either way the flagged gap (both called 'THE ranking', never
 compared) is now closed with data.

