 CORRECTED VERDICT: with both source-heavy, the Perron (spectral) and arborescence (combinatorial)
 centralities are strongly CORRELATED but NOT identical -- mean Kendall-tau high, exact-match only
 sometimes. So they are two DISTINCT-but-aligned centralities, and the divergence set (classes
 where they rank differently) is a new, small object worth isolating. (My first run used the LEFT
 Perron eigenvector -> weakness-heavy -> spurious near-reversal; corrected. Same direction trap as
 THM-1750, flagged.)

